{
  "credit": "LegendCraft — Cryomancer Ice Lance projectile skin (cryomancer.md 'Ice Lance', pattern D/B).",
  "comment_authoring": "Authored ALONG +Z with the TIP POINTING +Z, spanning z=1.0..15.0 (14.0u). The cross-section is centred on x=8, y=8 so an ItemDisplay rolls it about its own axis with no wobble. Silhouette = double-terminated crystal: small dark butt (1.0u) -> shaft 1.8u (the widest) with a 45deg-spun nested core ridge -> pale 1.2u taper step -> 0.6u frost-white point. Value runs dark at the butt to white at the point; the tip element is the model's ONE glow focal.",
  "comment_tip_offset": "TIP_OFFSET = 0.4375 blocks. The point sits +0.4375 blocks along the model's local +Z from the display origin (model space 8,8,8), measured at ItemDisplay scale 1.0 — multiply by any applied scale. Per vfx-seam-requirements.md A3 the projectile seam places the TIP at the collision point, so the visual offset is +0.4375 blocks forward along the travel axis. DECLARED ONCE HERE — do not re-derive per ability.",
  "comment_no_animation": "NOTHING in this model animates. The 0.3s crystallise-on-cast growth and the slow axial roll in flight are plugin-side interpolated ItemDisplay transforms (setInterpolationDuration + setTransformation); vanilla item models cannot express rotation over time and .mcmeta only animates texture frames.",
  "texture_size": [32, 32],
